# Google OAuth 2.0 — Quick Connect (shared) client credentials
# Used when user picks "Quick Connect" in onboarding (default path).
# BYO path uses user-provided credentials at runtime — no env needed.
#
# How to get these:
#   1. Create GCP project (https://console.cloud.google.com)
#   2. Enable APIs: Gmail API, Google Calendar API
#   3. Configure OAuth consent screen (External, Testing mode)
#   4. Add scopes: gmail.readonly, gmail.send, calendar.events
#   5. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type: "Desktop app")
#   6. Copy Client ID + Client Secret below
#   7. Save this file as .env.local (NOT .env.example) — .env.local is gitignored
#
# See: _workspace/2026-04/w3/google-workspace/adrs/ADR-001-oauth-strategy.md
# See: _workspace/2026-04/w3/google-workspace/github-issues/milestone-w1-oauth.md#W1-01

GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here
